<title>LUXEMBOURG: French cast doubt on EU reforms - sources.</title>
<headline>French cast doubt on EU reforms - sources.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The negotiating stance of the new French government casts doubt on the passage of reforms at the European Union summit in Amsterdam, EU sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;In the meeting, (French Finance Minister Dominique) Strauss-Kahn made it clear that there was a link to the Intergovernmental Conference,&quot; a senior EU source said.</p>
<p>Other diplomats confirmed that the French position could also entail demands to change the employment chapter of the new EU Treaty, due to be approved by heads of state and government at the Amsterdam Summit June 16-17.</p>
</text>
